We set grammar and mechanics rules to help our writers create clear, concise and consistent copy across all content types. This section explains our house style, which all our content follows unless client notes say differently. Always use client notes when available!

(Use Ctrl+F or the search feature to help you find what you’re looking for!)

# T**he Basics**

- **Write for all readers**. Whether your readers hang on to your every word or skim for the main points, use specific headings and subheadings to break up text and group similar ideas.
- **Follow the inverted pyramid technique.** Order your information so you lead with the most important information.
- **Be clear.** Avoid vague language or unnecessary jargon. Get to the point quickly.
    - Paragraphs should not be excessively long. White space is great! Break up excessively long sentences into two sentences for better readability.
- **Be concise.** Keep your words and sentences short, and pick simple words to make your point. Avoid unnecessary modifiers, and eradicate filler words from your writing.
    - Avoid repeating the same words and/or phrases in consecutive sentences.
- **Be consistent.** Closely follow the points detailed in this guide.

