## **Point of view**

Second person is the POV of choice, unless client notes or specs specify otherwise. For example, instead of “for those who enjoy” you can say “If you enjoy.” This makes it more personal and engaging. Another example is using “you” instead of “our customers” or “our clients.”

Aim to edit out “we” in posts whenever possible, apart from the CTA. For many forms of writing, switching point of view is often frowned upon, especially if you’ve been trained to pick a voice and stick with it.

For CTAs, however, **do** use first-person POV to write on behalf of the client — for example, saying “our company” instead of “the company.”

