## Recipes

For projects that collect recipes into one post, **reword the recipes so they are in your own words**. Repeating recipes verbatim causes duplicate copy and can make a project too long.

Instead, it’s generally best to put the ingredients and steps into sentences. Use numerals and fractions but not abbreviations: “2 teaspoons” not “two tsp.”

If we’re using the client’s recipes, include a link to the recipe page so readers can easily get the full details if they want. If it’s not the client’s recipe, link to it if it’s from an authoritative source, e.g. a food magazine rather than an individual’s blog.

