## **Numbers in keywords**

Sometimes, numbers will be formatted in keywords in a way that goes against typical AP style rules (such as “3 Wheel Forklifts”). In these cases, you can use numerals even for numbers under 10 in the subheads. Then, spell out the numbers like we typically would per AP Style in the body copy.

Example:

[H2] Looking for a 3-Wheel Forklift for Sale? Contact X Client

[Body text] If you’re in the market for an electric three-wheel forklift, X Client has you covered.

## **Dates**

Use figures for dates and years. Generally, spell out the day of the week and the month, capitalizing the month. Do not use endings like *st, nd, rd or th* (1st, 2nd, etc.)

– **Yes:** Saturday, January 24, 2012

– **No:** Sat., Jan. 24th

## **Decimals and fractions**

Spell out fractions, unless stating dimensions.

– **Yes:** two-thirds

– **No:** 2/3

– **Yes:** 8 3/4 inches

– **No:** eight and three-fourths inches

– **No:** 8-3/4 inches

Use decimal points when a number can’t be easily written out as a fraction, like 1.375 or 47.2. Always use numerals and a period to indicate decimal amounts. For amounts less than 1, use the numeral 0 before a decimal.

– **Yes:** 1.23

– **No:** one point two-three

