## H**yphens and dashes**

Use a hyphen (-) without spaces on either side to link words into single phrase, or to indicate a span or range.

– first-time user

– Monday-Friday

Use an em dash (—) with spaces on either side to signal a change in thought, a series within a phrase or to attribute a quote. Do not use the slightly narrower en dash.

– Walmart — the well-known retail giant — is the world's single largest employer.

– She made a list of all the things — like swimming, tanning and sight-seeing — that she wanted to do on her vacation.

**How to make the em dash:**

- Press Ctrl+Alt+Minus (on the numeric keypad)
- On a Mac, you can hit Shift + Option + Hyphen
- On a PC, you can hold down the Alt key as you type 0151 on the numeric keypad
- Choose Symbol from the Insert menu, and then select Em Dash from the Special Characters tab.

